# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ishtar workspace - line-ending policy
#
# Written by Faz 1.1 (Version Control Bootstrap).
#
# This host has core.autocrlf=true. Left alone, git would check out every
# tracked text file with CRLF line endings. That is not merely cosmetic here:
# ishtar-cam-modes ships shell scripts that are executed by the on-device
# Magisk shell at post-fs-data, and a CRLF script fails there in ways that are
# slow and confusing to diagnose. The whole point of this repository is that a
# checkout restores a working file, so conversion has to be pinned, not left
# to a per-machine git setting.
#
# Policy, in two parts:
#   1. Default to no conversion at all. The repository is a recovery tool
#      first; a checkout must return the same bytes that were committed,
#      whatever they were. The workspace currently holds a mix of LF and CRLF
#      files and this preserves each one as it stands.
#   2. Force LF for the artifacts that are consumed by a Linux or Android
#      shell, or by the patch tooling. All of these are already LF today, so
#      this pins the current state rather than rewriting anything.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Default: byte-preserving.
* -text

# 2. Must be LF, because something outside Windows reads them.
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.prop   text eol=lf
*.patch  text eol=lf
mode     text eol=lf
lang     text eol=lf
